  "title": "The business impact of synthetic identity fraud and why prevention requires a lifecycle approach",
  "summary": "Synthetic identity fraud challenges banks, fintechs and other institutions at the financial, operational, and strategic level. It causes losses that are real but often invisible, buried in credit line loss metrics that obscure the fraud behind them. The fraud controls that organizations believe are sufficiently protecting them are often insufficient to meet the nature of this threat, and the prevention strategies that actually work require a total rethink of how identity is managed throughout customer relationships, rather than just at onboarding.",
